    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 6716fad19583a9a8cfafe45826058a8e2754ef3b -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\nReviewed at head 6716fad1, trial-merged with current origin/main (clean).\n\n**What looks good**\n- One history step per box: the UI `finish` (`crates/ui/src/box_pick.rs`) queues one `SetOperationGeometry` with the existing picks plus the new ones, and the MCP `pick_in_box` (`crates/app/src/mcp/box_pick.rs`) runs one `SetOperationGeometry` through `history.execute`. Undo restores the previous selection (`mcp_pick_in_box_adds_the_rim_in_one_undo_step`).\n- The drag is ephemeral: `State.pick_box` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`) is set only while the pointer is down, and it is never a command.\n- Degenerate input takes nothing and adds no step: `Rect::of` refuses a zero or non-finite box, `box_bodies` refuses a zero view direction (`crates/app/src/pick/box_pick.rs:205-240`). A zero-size UI drag reports \"no visible ... the box\" without a command. The MCP refuses a zero-area box by message.\n- The visibility rule is the click pick's own (`feature_pick::occluded`), feature chains and welded faces only, and hidden features are not picked through (`through: false`). Stock and fixtures are excluded as candidates.\n- Layering: the app owns the geometry rule (`pick::box_select`, `box_select_top`), and the UI only arms the gesture and routes the result.\n- No snapshot PNG in the diff. `docs/decisions/979-box-select-picks.md` is present, and the body has `Changelog:` and `Fixes #979`.\n- `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic` appear only in test files.\n\n**Local results (trial merge with main)**\n| Suite | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test box_pick` | 6 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib box_select` (CWD crates/ui) | 2 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib structural` (CWD crates/ui) | 4 passed, 0 failed |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean |\n\n**Requested before merge**\nNone.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n1. `crates/ui/src/box_pick.rs` `picks_in` and `finish` pass `&state.world` into app helpers (`pick::box_select`, `model::find_by_name`). The same pattern is already used by other UI modules (for example `crates/ui/src/actions.rs`), so it matches the current code. A future cleanup could move this into an app seam.\n2. `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs` was already 960 lines on main and is now 983. It is over the 400-line guide, but the growth is small.\n3. The MCP `replace: true` path with a selection identical to the current one still writes a history step. It is harmless, but a no-op step is not needed.\n4. If the pointer is released outside the viewport during a box drag, `pick_box` keeps its last corner, so the box is taken at that corner. Worth a check in the GUI.\n5. Not exercised: real window rubber-band look; the cost of up to 16 sight rays per candidate on large meshes (the PR says it was not timed).\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
